PATCH 360: the editor .FSG battle-SAVE serializer -- FUN_0000_d6e4 (DCBS unit-chunk writer) + its
count pass FUN_0000_d84e + its per-unit pre-walk dispatch FUN_0000_d740 + the unit list-unlink
FUN_0000_b40b + the .FSW/.FSE filename builder FUN_0000_d638 (asm 0xd6e4 / 0xd84e / 0xd740 / 0xb40b
/ 0xd638) -- the variable-length + side-file parts of FUN_0000_d5f9.  The fixed-size chunk writers
(SHDR d683, PATH d788, STMP d797, PINF d76a, BINF d779, TERM d7a6) are load-into-place /
save-from-place and already faithful; DCBS alone is written by walking the live unit list via the
c157/c164 iterator (patch 168), and the .FSW/.FSE names are built by rewriting the extension char.

Ghidra base-lost all five: it folded c164's returned near-offset (si) + end-of-list CF into spurious
host-ptr walks of the unused param args (`*param_1`, `param_1[-0xce8]`) -> the 0x79a9 filename
near-offset host-deref SIGSEGV; in d6e4 it also mangled the `push ax; push si` / `pop dx; pop cx`
around the unit-data write into `param_4`/uStack0002 -> a 0-length + wild write; b40b (dispatched by
d740 for class-0x1b units) deref'd the node near-offset di as a host pointer (byte[di+0x16] -> the
0xa038 SIGSEGV) with a host-int mis-scaled stride-2 list scan; and d638 assigned the uint16
near-offset a96e to a `char*` and walked it as a host pointer.  All reconstructed faithfully via the
established c164/g_fist_cf idiom (cf. d755 patch 169) and the DGROUP-near-offset memory model; the
per-unit bcc4 index/value lookup (FUN_1000_b354) is inlined in d6e4 because the shared b354 decompile
returns only the index (drops DX) and, with a host 4-byte int, mis-scales its stride/deref.  d740's
reached slots are the no-op c30e (classes 0/1) and b40b (class 0x1b, touches only the transient
5ccf/5cd7 lists, not the serialized unit bytes); d651 (called by d638) only creates a .FSW/.FSE when
one is missing (AH=4300 get-attr gate), so existing side files are preserved.

Reached only by the editor .FSG SAVE path (d5f9 / the 361 round-trip harness), unreached by the 26
verify flows -> behaviour-neutral for them.  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.

